{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QVcMFUirZz1yCYL8K4Wv31","type":"tool_result","content":"  `npm run test:live`); each passes with a \"skipped\" note when its\n  `ROAST_LIVE_*` key is unset, so the TAP stream is never empty.\n\n## Differential harness (`test/diff/`, deleted at M6)\n\n- `npm run test:diff` runs the harness self-tests (no Go needed), then\n  every scenario against the Go baseline built at `cd08f10` into\n  `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff/` (delete it to force a rebuild).\n  Without `go` on `PATH` every scenario is a TAP skip.\n- Add a milestone's scenarios as a `Scenario[]` under\n  `test/diff/scenarios/` and list it in `SCENARIOS` (`index.ts`);\n  `server`, `records`, and `requests` turn on the fake server and\n  record/request comparison.\n- A difference caused by a deliberate change goes in `ALLOWLIST`\n  (`allowlist.ts`) naming the change number. Go behavior judged wrong\n  goes in the owning area's Open questions, never patched in the\n  harness.\n- Review scenarios script the fake with `scriptedServer` (`replies.ts`),\n  keyed by `<model>#<turns>` like the request groups. A first finder\n  call has 3 messages, a first verifier call 2; an unscripted key gets\n  a 404 naming it. Credential variables must not start with a scrubbed\n  prefix (`ROAST_`, `OPENAI_`, ...): `scrubbedEnv` drops them.\n- Go-only incidental bytes are normalized, not allowlisted: SDK headers\n  (`X-Stainless-*`), Go's `\\u003c` HTML escaping (records compare as\n  parsed JSON, including `provider-responses.jsonl`), gzip/zstd bytes\n  and the bundle-manifest hashes of compressed members, finding UUIDs\n  and aliases, and the snapshot `commit` / `ref` OIDs.\n- Self-tests that need a one-sided difference wrap the TS CLI: a node\n  script that edits records after `dist/cli.js` exits, or `node\n  --import <hook>` replacing `globalThis.fetch` (the adapters send a\n  `Uint8Array` body).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session