{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM2Bp4VXihpVp8trBu5P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run test:diff` runs the `runs` listing scenarios. Go and TS agree on exit code and parsed JSON stdout after normalization.\n[x] `npm run test:diff` runs the `runs checkout` scenario. Both CLIs exit the same and produce the same file set and contents in the target directory, with no denylisted file present.\n[x] `npm run test:diff` runs the `runs prune` scenarios (dry run and real). Both CLIs exit the same and leave the same snapshot refs.\n[x] `npm run test:diff` runs the `init` scenario. Both CLIs exit the same and write parsed-equal `.roast.json` and equal `.gitignore`.\n[x] Every allowlist entry added here cites the spec.md deliberate change it covers. No scenario passes only because of a broad ignore rule.\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nI've added the 13 M5 scenarios to the differential harness, and every one matches the Go baseline locally with no allowlist entries. One checklist item is still open: the harness CI job will not pass yet, because of 8 M3 scenarios that were already failing before this ticket.\n\n**The scenarios** (`test/diff/scenarios/m5.ts`):\n- **Listing:** `runs`, `runs --json`, `runs --limit 1 --json` and `runs show <id>`, each after two reviews against the fake server. `runs` and `runs show` compare exit codes only, because their output is human text and rendered Markdown, which the spec says not to compare.\n- **Checkout:** `runs checkout <id> ../checkout` compares the file set and contents. The fixture has an untracked `notes.txt`, which must be checked out, and `server.pem`, `id_rsa` and `creds.txt`, which must not.\n- **Prune:** `runs prune --dry-run` and `runs prune --older-than 24h` compare the remaining `refs/roast/snapshots/*`. The second review's snapshot is dated 2099, so the real prune removes exactly one ref.\n- **Init:** three runs of `init --no-login`: OpenAI and Anthropic model IDs, OpenRouter `vendor/model` IDs with a `.gitignore` that has no final newline, and an unplaceable model (exit 2 on both). Each compares `.roast.json`, parsed as JSONC, and the `.gitignore` text.\n\n**Runner changes** (`test/diff/scenario.ts`): scenarios can now run setup commands first (their exit codes are compared), and the command under test can use that side's own run IDs. Beyond stdout, a scenario can also compare:\n- the line-by-line JSON output of `runs --json`\n- a checked-out directory, plus files that must be absent from it\n- refs under a prefix, with each run ID replaced by its position\n- files written into the repository\n\n**Self-tests** (`test/diff/selftest/m5.ts`) run without Go. Each scenario compares equal TS against TS, and a difference planted on one side gets reported at the right path: a dropped index line, an extra checked-out file, a denylisted file, a deleted ref, a changed model ID.\n\n**Why the CI item is open:** the 8 failing M3 scenarios all differ only because TS sends the `__roast_continue` tool in request bodies and Go does not. That is the open question ticket 26 recorded in spec 07, and it needs your decision. The M5 scenarios don't compare requests, so they aren't affected. I also haven't run CI itself, only the harness on macOS.\n\n**Checks:** lint passes, `npm test` passes all 7127 tests, and the Go build and `npm run test:go` pass.\n\nI added harness notes to `docs/agents/typescript.md`. Everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":124758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1023},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,